    "closed": [
      "Clone is a read-only current-ACL query; new local clock, uncleared/unreviewed defaults, no IDs/source key/occurrence or financial writes until Save. Current source and linked-fee authority is rechecked; new archived/hidden assignments refuse.",
      "Exact amounts, rounded historical FX quote and original instant are retained in new form seeds. Split rows/default labels remain editable without floating point money; pending intent and session ownership use the existing command owner.",
      "Clone read/loading blocks competing commands, rejects late generation/disposal and revalidates source before exposing a draft. Later source grant revocation purges an open cloned draft, including a changed private fee link.",
      "Allocation replacement uses one I01 transaction, exact positive signed64 strings, distinct categories, bounded100 rows and exact sum to one income/expense posting. No second posting or amount duplication. No-ops, stale revisions and same-key replay retain original authority semantics.",
      "Atomic create/update/clone carries allocation rows and preserves money/category/label/source policy. Native second-row failure rolls back record/postings/metadata/audit/nonce; amount and split changes either commit together or refuse.",
      "Current read authority, matching revision and exact total are required for split manifests. Unknown split payload/key survives navigation and explicit retry; competing editors/bulk are blocked, conflicts require explicit reload and refresh synchronously drops public rows/forms.",
      "New explicit schema7/standalone8 adds owned-template storage and strict split validation. Accepted1-6 DDL/checksum bytes and historical backup conversion remain; inconsistent legacy splits block explicit upgrade without repair. No automatic migration or activation.",
      "Category filtering/search and cross-page selection use split children once, omit unrelated parent category and withhold private/partial split associations. Internal index IDs never enter public query DTO; cursor revision fences remain.",
      "Existing bulk/selection/catalog fixtures are explicitly pinned6, preserving their original schema assertions after the registry gained7. Default4/receipt5/bulk6 remain; workflow7 fixture is separate and offline with closed handles.",
      "Native browser first26/27 failed before the final financial action: its source was outside the first50 of68 rows. DOM/trace retained; new-case setup now scopes synthetic sources before selection, retaining every assertion/selector/deadline and all23 parent titles. Final28 includes split-clone atomic creation."
